    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Associate-Registrar--Student-Governance-and-Compliance_R31044-2": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar, Student Governance and Compliance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-07\nFull time\n\nWho we are ?   At Torrens University Australia,   making a difference is in our DNA.   As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world.   That’s   why   we’re   on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all   walks of life   can chase their dreams.       Just like our students,   our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact . When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold,   creative   and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best.   We’ve   built a culture that celebrates community,   collaboration   and innovation, where people love what they do .       What’s the job?     The Associate Registrar   -   Student Governance and Compliance provides senior governance,   assurance   and regulatory oversight across designated Academic Services functions. The role supports the integrity of student decision-making, academic records, complaints and appeals, student safety and wellbeing processes,   completions   and related student administration.     Working across Academic Services, Student Experience, Legal, Risk,   Compliance   and academic areas, you will ensure processes are fair, consistent, evidence-based,   compliant   and auditable. You will lead or coordinate complex and high-risk matters within delegated authority, provide constructive   challenges   to operational   leaders   and advise senior stakeholders on regulatory obligations, risk,   assurance   and continuous improvement.     D ay - to - day accountabilities :   Provide governance and assurance oversight across student complaints, appeals,   misconduct   and academic integrity processes, ensuring procedural fairness and   appropriate separation   of investigation, decision-making,   review   and appeal functions.   Lead complex and high-risk matters within delegated authority,   maintaining   confidentiality, privacy, records   management   and conflict-of-interest requirements.   Coordinate the University’s responses to external complaints and investigations, including matters referred to the National Student Ombudsman, and prepare evidence-based submissions and response materials.   Oversee student wellbeing and safety processes, including escalation, reporting, referrals, incident   management   and compliance with gender-based violence prevention and response requirements.   Maintain evidence readiness, data   integrity   and audit compliance, using student voice, case   trends   and emerging risks to drive continuous improvement, particularly for students at risk and under-represented cohorts.   Establish and   maintain   a risk-based assurance framework across complaints, student safety, completions,   records   and student administration processes.   Translate legislative and regulatory requirements into clear policies, procedures, controls, evidence   requirements   and escalation pathways, including ESOS, the National Code, TEQSA, ASQA, HESF, CRICOS and PRISMS obligations.   Lead reporting on complaints, student   safety   and wellbeing, GBV, completions,   graduation   and related student administration matters, ensuring information is   accurate , privacy compliant and audit ready.   Provide oversight and assurance of completions, award eligibility, certification, graduation, student records and post-enrolment processes including progression, re-enrolment, transfers, withdrawals,   credit   and recognition of prior learning.   Provide expert advice to senior leaders and governance forums, work with Heads of Department and key stakeholders to resolve issues, and address root causes through policy review and continuous improvement.   Lead and develop a high-performing team, fostering accountability, accuracy, service, collaboration,   learning   and positive leadership.   Who you are   A postgraduate qualification in a relevant discipline, or equivalent professional experience.   Significant senior experience in academic or student administration within higher education.   Demonstrated experience managing student complaints,   appeals   and complex case resolution, including high-risk matters.   Experience leading responses to external complaints,   investigations   or regulatory bodies.   Experience overseeing student lifecycle processes, including progression, academic   records   and completions.   Advanced knowledge of the Australian higher education regulatory framework, including the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, with the ability to translate obligations into fair and auditable processes.   Strong working knowledge of the ESOS Act, National Code, TEQSA, ASQA, HESF, CRICOS and PRISMS requirements.   Experience providing leadership or assurance in student wellbeing and safety, including sensitive disclosures, incident response,   risk   and gender-based violence compliance.   Strong analytical, reporting and data governance skills, with the ability to use digital tools and AI appropriately to improve workflows, case   management   and service delivery.   Sound judgement, problem-solving, stakeholder engagement,   communication   and influencing skills, with the ability to deliver fair,   practical   and student-centred outcomes.     To read more about the role please   click here .   This is a permanent, full-time position   based   at Surry Hills Campus in Sydney.     Why join us?     Bold,   modern   and agile,   we’re   Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020,   Australian Financial Review   named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to   establish   ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people,   you’ll   find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression.      We are proud to be an   e qual opportunity employer   and   committed   to creating an inclusive workplace.   We do not discriminate   on the basis of   race, colour, religion,   age,   ethnicity,   gender identity, sexual orientation ,   disability , or any other protected characteristic.      We   encourage   applications from   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people s for all positions.       What we offer :   We support your personal passions,   development   and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At    Torrens University   Australia,   you’ll   benefit   from:       Study free in a course/degree related to your position       B Corp certified university – values   driven,   and purpose led   Access to internal opportunities - Be supported to learn,   grow   and move across the organisation           Hiring process     We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at   your career @torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring   an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.    To learn more about   what makes Torrens University Australia   a great place   to work, visit   https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .     We’d love to hear from you.     Job   r eference:   R31044     Applications for this role will close on   Wednesday 30 th   September.     Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be   identified . You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates   regarding   your application.   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
