    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Work-Health-and-Safety-Manager_R31159-1": {
      "title": "Work Health and Safety Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.   Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do.   What’s the job?   As the Work Health and Safety Manager , you’ll lead the planning, implementation and continuous improvement of work health and safety across Torrens Global Education and its related entities. Acting as a trusted consultant to all levels of staff, you’ll promote safe working practices, strengthen awareness and help ensure compliance with legislation and workplace obligations.   You’ll partner with business units and leaders to identify and manage physical and psychological risks, provide practical advice and maintain effective health and safety frameworks. The role also manages work-related and non-work-related injuries, workers compensation claims, reporting, training, incident investigations and WHS projects across the organisation.   You’ll help foster a culture of safety awareness and accountability by encouraging open communication, timely reporting and participation in safety initiatives. Working closely with HR, campus, risk and project teams, you’ll support measurable safety improvements and maintain the organisation’s readiness to meet its regulatory and compliance responsibilities.   Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to):   Partner with business units to provide advice on safe workplace obligations, frameworks, tools and legislation, helping teams mitigate physical and psychological risks.   Manage work-related and non-work-related injuries end to end and effectively manage workers compensation claims to support employees and mitigate organisational risk.   Manage the annual renewal of workers compensation premiums, assess cost drivers and identify opportunities for improvement.   Develop, coordinate and maintain WHS frameworks, policies, records and information across the organisation.   Monitor legislative changes and maintain ongoing compliance with WHS requirements, including relevant regulatory standards and codes of practice.   Develop and deliver health and safety training for key stakeholders.   Collaborate with department managers to investigate accidents, incidents and near misses and recommend corrective actions to prevent recurrence.     Who you are   A WHS professional with qualifications in work health and safety and/or at least six years’ experience in this specialist area.   A holder of a Return to Work Coordinator certificate for South Australia.   Experienced in applying WHS legislation, regulations and codes of practice in a complex organisation.   Experienced in managing work-related injuries, workers compensation claims and end-to-end case management.   A confident project lead with experience delivering work health and safety initiatives and practical improvements.   A strong communicator and relationship builder who can consult effectively with leaders, employees and diverse stakeholders.   Highly organised and self-directed, with the ability to manage competing priorities and day-to-day workflow under broad supervision.   To read more about the role please click here .   This is a full-time, permanent position offering hybrid flexibility, with the opportunity to work from home and from one of our campuses. Preferred location Sydney or Melbourne we are also open to Adelaide and Brisbane location for this role.   Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression.   We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.   We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.   What we offer:   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:   Study free in a course/degree related to your position   Make a measurable impact on employee wellbeing and workplace safety   A purpose-driven workplace that values community, collaboration and innovation   Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.   If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.   To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog.   We’d love to hear from you.   Job reference: R31159   Applications for this role will close on Sunday 18th October. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Senior-Project-Manager_R31184-1": {
      "title": "Senior Project Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nSenior Project Manager  Fixed-Term | Sydney | Hybrid flexible working Who We Are   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams. Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration and innovation, where people love what they do.  What’s the Job? We are seeking an experienced Senior Project Manager to lead the integrated delivery of the University’s Banner SaaS implementation and associated business transformation programme. This is a high-profile, enterprise-wide role that will bring together University teams, implementation partners, system integrators and third-party vendors. You will establish the structure, governance and delivery discipline required to move a complex programme forward and support successful implementation across the University. You will lead programme planning, governance, reporting, risk and dependency management, vendor coordination, testing, cutover and operational readiness. You will work closely with accountable functional, technical, data, integration, testing, training and change leads to ensure all parts of the programme are aligned and progressing. You will not be expected to be the technical subject-matter expert across every domain. However, you will need sufficient understanding of enterprise systems, integrations, data and technology delivery to identify risks, challenge assumptions and coordinate effective decisions. This is a 12 months fixed-term opportunity based at our Surry Hills campus in Sydney, with hybrid flexibility. Key Responsibilities (but not limited to): Lead a foundational platform / programme plan, including milestones, dependencies, resources, decisions and critical path activities.  Align programme delivery with university priorities, expected benefits, portfolio planning, and organisational outcomes. Establish and operate effective governance, executive reporting, assurance, and escalation processes. Coordinate functional, technical, data, integration, security, testing, training and change workstreams. Manage scope, requirements, risks, issues, dependencies, change control, and formal approvals. Act as the University’s primary day-to-day contact for implementation partners, system integrators and third-party vendors. Monitor vendor deliverables, performance, resourcing, service levels, commercial obligations, and escalations. Coordinate migration, technical readiness, and dependencies across the University’s wider digital ecosystem. Lead integrated testing, cutover and operational-readiness planning, ensuring workstream owners are prepared for implementation. Support regulatory compliance, benefits realisation, continuous improvement and the uplift of project delivery capability across the University. Who You Are   You are a calm, structured and outcomes-focused programme professional who is comfortable working in complex, matrixed environments. You bring clarity to competing priorities, communicate complex issues plainly and build confidence through transparency and follow-through. You will bring: Demonstrated experience leading complex enterprise technology, SaaS, student information system or business transformation programmes. Direct Ellucian Banner experience is highly desirable. Experience with another higher education platform or large-scale enterprise system will also be considered. Strong experience in programme planning, governance, risk, issue, dependency and change management. Demonstrated experience coordinating system integration, data migration, testing, cutover and operational readiness across multiple workstreams. Proven experience managing implementation partners, system integrators and third-party vendors, including delivery commitments, performance, resourcing and escalations. Strong stakeholder-management and communication skills, with the ability to influence executives, academic leaders, technical specialists, operational teams and external partners. Experience working in a matrix environment with distributed or international teams. The ability to make sound decisions with incomplete information, challenge constructively and maintain momentum through ambiguity. Relevant project or programme management qualifications. PMP, PRINCE2, MSP or an equivalent certification would be highly regarded. Why Join Us? This is an opportunity to lead a significant enterprise transformation with genuine organisational reach. You will work across technology, operations, academic and leadership teams while helping shape the platforms and digital ecosystem that support the University’s future. At Torrens University Australia, you will benefit from: A purpose-led, B Corp-certified organisation. Flexible hybrid working arrangements. The opportunity to lead a complex, high-profile transformation with global stakeholders. Access to professional development and internal career opportunities. The opportunity to study free in a course related to your position, subject to eligibility requirements. A collaborative and inclusive working environment. Our Commitment to Inclusion We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and are committed to creating an inclusive, accessible and equitable workplace. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and people from all backgrounds. If you require adjustments or additional support during the recruitment process, please contact yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential assistance. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog . We’d love to hear from you.     Job reference: R31184 To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on Sunday 18 October. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with any updates about your applications. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Academic-Registrar-and-Senior-Director-Academic-Services_R31166-1": {
      "title": "Academic Registrar and Senior Director Academic Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nWho we are:   At Torrens University Australia , making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.    A progressive university, we ground our studies in industry. Expert academics bring their insights into the classroom, with a range of assessment types that aim to be authentic and informed by industry needs. Bridging the gap between study and work, our educators prepare students for career success and connect them with future employers. Building relevant skills, experience and networks from day one, students don’t just learn about their industry, they live it.    What’s the job?   The Academic Registrar and Senior Director Academic Services is the university's senior leader for Academic Services. The role provides strategic leadership across the university's academic services ecosystem, setting portfolio-wide direction, service standards, planning frameworks, assurance and performance expectations.  The role leads student academic services and academic administration across the student lifecycle, including academic records, progression and completion, graduations, subject and course logistics, academic systems, complaints and appeals, student safety and wellbeing compliance, academic data processing and support for academic enquiries.  You will be accountable for the integrity, security, accuracy and effectiveness of academic records, student administration, academic governance, planning, complaints, appeals, student information systems, data and delivery readiness. The role connects three portfolios: student governance, compliance and academic services assurance; academic governance and administration; and academic planning and operations.    Principle accountabilities (but not limited to):   Senior Leadership and Portfolio Governance - lead Academic Services by setting strategic priorities, service standards, accountabilities and performance expectations across the three-portfolio operating model.  Academic Governance, Policy and Quality - lead academic governance and quality processes, ensuring academic rules, regulatory requirements, reporting frameworks and escalation pathways support sound decisions and continuous improvement.  Registrar, Complaints, Appeals and Independent Assurance - provide senior oversight of the assurance function, complaints, appeals, procedural fairness and student wellbeing and safety risks while protecting independence and impartiality.  Records, Results, Completions and Graduation - oversee the accuracy, security and integrity of student outcomes, academic records, results, completions, certification, conferral and graduation processes across the student lifecycle  Academic Planning, Timetabling and Delivery Readiness - lead integrated academic planning, timetabling and delivery readiness using demand, capacity, progression and workforce data to identify risks and support timely decisions.  Systems, Data and Continuous Improvement - drive continuous improvement across Academic Services systems, processes, data and workflow by strengthening automation, data quality, controls, integrations, security and vendor delivery.  Who you are:   Senior leader with extensive higher education, VET or dual-sector experience across academic services, registry, governance, planning and operations.  Experienced in academic planning, forecasting, timetabling, delivery readiness, systems, data and process improvement.  Experienced in overseeing student wellbeing and safety, including sensitive matters, high-risk issues and regulatory obligations.  Trusted adviser who can influence senior leaders and governance bodies across complex organisational structures.  Accomplished people leader skilled in building high-performing teams, accountability and organisational change.  Strong knowledge of the Australian tertiary regulatory environment, including HESF, TEQSA, ASQA, ESOS, the National Code, CRICOS, VET, privacy and data requirements.  Strong institutional judgement and data-led capability in assurance, reporting, continuous improvement, automation, and AI.  Collaborative, student-centred and solutions-focused, with confidence to challenge established practice constructively.  Exceptional communicator with strong attention to detail, accuracy and student information systems literacy.  Qualifications   Relevant postgraduate or professional qualification in education, higher education, business, governance, public administration, law or related discipline.  Certificate IV in Training and Assessment (TAE40110 or TAE40116), or equivalent contemporary credential, is desirable where relevant.  Professional qualification or certification in academic governance, compliance, risk, quality, or public administration is desirable.    To read more about the role please click here .   This is a permanent, full-time position. The preferred location for this role is at our Surry Hills campus in Sydney. Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we are Australia's fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country's most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you will find opportunities for professional development and career progression.  We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.  We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.  What we offer:   Study free in a course or degree related to your position.  B Corp certified university - values driven and purpose led.  Access to internal opportunities - be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation.  A collaborative, student-focused environment where you can help shape the future of academic services.    Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .    We’d love to hear from you.  Job reference: R31166  To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on Wednesday 4th November.    Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Senior-Application-Engineer---Salesforce_R31192-2": {
      "title": "Senior Application Engineer - Salesforce",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nWho we are? At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams. Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration and innovation, where people love what they do. About the role: We’re looking for a Senior Application Engineer - Salesforce to play a critical role in the development, implementation and maintenance of our Salesforce CRM and Marketing Cloud platforms within a complex, integrated environment. This role focuses on building and supporting integrations between Salesforce and our Student Management System, Banner, using Informatica, along with a range of other connected systems. You’ll bring strong Salesforce development experience, a solid understanding of CRM and marketing automation, and a hands-on approach to coding, configuration and troubleshooting. Working closely with teams across the organisation, you’ll help deliver practical, scalable and high-quality solutions that support business outcomes, improve user experience and strengthen the way our platforms operate. Key accountabilities (but not limited to): Salesforce development & customisation: Design, build and enhance Salesforce CRM and Marketing Cloud solutions using Apex, Lightning (Aura and LWC) and configuration best practice. System configuration & maintenance: Configure, maintain and continuously improve Salesforce environments to support business operations, system performance, reliability and user experience. Integrations & connected systems: Deliver and support robust integrations between Salesforce, Banner and other enterprise systems using REST and SOAP APIs, platform events, webhooks, middleware and integration platforms including Informatica. Marketing Cloud & AI enablement: Lead development and optimisation across Marketing Cloud, including Email Studio, Journey Builder, Automation Studio, Contact Builder, AMPscript and SQL, while staying informed about Agentforce, Einstein, Data Cloud and other AI capabilities. Hands-on technical leadership: Troubleshoot complex issues, perform root-cause analysis, provide production support and continuously improve performance, scalability, reliability, security and engineering quality across the Salesforce ecosystem. Quality assurance & engineering practices: Apply secure coding practices, peer review, unit testing, integration testing and Salesforce platform best practice to deliver high-quality, maintainable solutions with reduced defects. Release & environment management: Support controlled Salesforce deployments across development, testing and production environments using GitLab, including validation, documentation, rollback planning and minimal disruption to business operations.   Collaboration & solution design: Work closely with IT, Marketing, Student Services, Product Owners, business analysts, QA, release and support teams to understand business needs, translate them into technical solutions and deliver outcomes that are fit-for-purpose and future-ready.   Documentation, training & strategic planning: Maintain accurate technical documentation, deliver training and knowledge sharing, and contribute to the IT roadmap, platform continuous improvement, technical debt reduction and engineering maturity. Who you are: You’re a senior Salesforce engineer who is deeply technical, analytical and hands-on by nature, with the communication skills to work confidently with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. You’ll bring: A tertiary qualification or formal training in IT, Computing Studies, Information Systems or a related discipline. At least five years of hands-on Salesforce development experience, preferably in an enterprise or higher education environment. Demonstrated experience with Apex, SOQL, Lightning Web Components, Flow, Visualforce, Aura, custom objects and fields, data modelling and Salesforce security. Experience with Salesforce Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Experience Cloud and Marketing Cloud, including Email Studio, Journey Builder, Automation Studio, Contact Builder, AMPscript and SQL. Proven experience designing and supporting Salesforce integrations using REST, SOAP, platform events, middleware and integration platforms such as Informatica. Knowledge of Salesforce authentication, sharing, profiles, permission sets, governor limits, performance considerations and secure integration patterns. Experience with CI/CD and release tools such as GitLab, Azure DevOps, Gearset, Copado or equivalent. Salesforce Platform Developer I certification, which is required. Platform Developer II, Administrator, Platform App Builder, Marketing Cloud or Architect certifications are desirable. Knowledge of Agentforce, Einstein, Salesforce AI capabilities or Data Cloud is desirable. Strong troubleshooting, analytical, communication and stakeholder-management skills, with experience working in Agile or similar delivery methodologies. Experience participating in code reviews, technical design reviews, testing, release planning and production support. Formal Salesforce certifications (Platform Developer, Marketing Cloud) are highly regarded, but your depth of hands-on capability and problem-solving mindset matter most.  This is a full-time, permanent position with hybrid flexibility to work from home and a campus near you. Preferred locations are Sydney and Melbourne.  To review the full job description please 'Click Here’ .   Why join us? Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, with 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and more than 2,000 staff. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions. What we offer: We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from: Study free in a course or degree related to your position Access to internal opportunities – be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation A collaborative, purpose-driven working environment where your work can make a meaningful difference Hiring process: We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact us at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog. We’d love to hear from you. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Academic-Services-Compliance-and-Reporting-Specialist_R31277-2": {
      "title": "Academic Services Compliance and Reporting Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nWho we are:   At Torrens University Australia , making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.    A progressive university, we ground our studies in industry. Expert academics bring their insights into the classroom, with a range of assessment types that aim to be authentic and informed by industry needs. Bridging the gap between study and work, our educators prepare students for career success and connect them with future employers. Building relevant skills, experience and networks from day one, students don’t just learn about their industry, they live it.    What’s the job?   The Academic Services Compliance and Reporting Specialist supports the Associate Registrar, Student Governance and Compliance, by coordinating compliance, risk, assurance, reporting and business improvement activities across Academic Administration Services and Student Experience. You will help maintain reliable governance information and evidence, support the implementation of regulatory and policy requirements, and provide reporting and analysis that assists risk management, assurance and service improvement. The role also provides delegated operational support for external complaints and National Student Ombudsman matters, escalating complex or high-risk issues to the Associate Registrar.    Principle accountabilities (but not limited to): Compliance, Risk and Assurance: manage compliance, risk and assurance activities, maintain registers and evidence repositories, conduct assurance reviews, and track corrective actions. Reporting, Data Quality and Performance: prepare quarterly reports, validate data, identify trends and anomalies, and maintain reporting documentation and evidence trails. External Complaints and National Student Ombudsman: coordinate complaints and investigations, prepare evidence-based responses, monitor deadlines, and track outcomes and remedial actions. Implementation and Business Improvement: coordinate compliance and improvement initiatives, including policies, processes, controls, milestones, dependencies, risks and stakeholder consultation. Student-Centred Insight and Responsible AI: analyse student feedback, complaints and service trends, and use approved digital and AI tools responsibly to support improvement and reporting. Who you are:   An experienced compliance, risk, assurance, reporting or business improvement professional who has worked in a complex or regulated environment, preferably higher education, vocational education or a comparable sector. Experienced in coordinating projects or improvement initiatives from planning through to implementation and follow-through. Confident maintaining risk registers, action plans, controls, evidence, reporting schedules and data-quality processes. Skilled in preparing reports, dashboards or briefing materials that identify trends, quantify activity and support sound decision-making. Experienced in coordinating sensitive complaints, regulatory investigations or National Student Ombudsman matters, including evidence collation, stakeholder coordination and deadline management. A clear and concise written communicator with strong analytical capability, attention to detail and confidence working with data, trends, metrics and quality checks. Able to exercise sound judgement, identify matters requiring escalation and follow issues through to resolution. Collaborative and student-centred, with the ability to build constructive relationships and coordinate contributions across multiple teams without direct authority. Digitally confident, including the responsible use of reporting tools, workflow systems and artificial intelligence with human oversight. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in business, education, law, governance, compliance, risk, quality, data, student administration or a related discipline, or equivalent relevant professional experience. Qualifications or professional development in compliance, risk, audit, quality assurance, project management, data analysis or business improvement are desirable. To read more about the role please click here . This is a permanent, full-time position. The preferred location for this role is at our Surry Hills campus in Sydney. Other campus locations may be considered (Brisbane, Melbourne, Adelaide).  Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we are Australia's fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country's most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you will find opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions. What we offer: Study free in a course or degree related to your position. B Corp certified university - values driven and purpose led. Access to internal opportunities - be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation. A collaborative, student-focused environment where you can help shape the future of academic services.  Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .    We’d love to hear from you. Job reference: R31277 To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on 12 November 2026. Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    }
  },
